      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please add a unit test in `test/fpsensor_crypto_with_mock.cc` exercising `MOCK_CTRL_FPSENSOR_CRYPTO_HKDF_SHA256_TYPE_FAIL` (alongside the existing tests for `MOCK_CTRL_FPSENSOR_CRYPTO_HKDF_SHA256_TYPE_ZEROS` and `MOCK_CTRL_FPSENSOR_CRYPTO_HKDF_SHA256_TYPE_FF`) so that this new failure branch and its `EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN` propagation in `derive_key()` are covered by `make run-fpsensor_crypto_with_mock`.\n\nFor example, in `test/fpsensor_crypto_with_mock.cc`:\n\n```cpp\ntest_static int test_derive_encryption_key_failure_hkdf_fail()\n{\n\tFpEncryptionKey unused_key{};\n\tconstexpr std::array\u003cuint8_t, FP_CONTEXT_ENCRYPTION_SALT_BYTES\u003e\n\t\tunused_salt{};\n\tconstexpr std::array\u003cuint8_t, FP_CONTEXT_USERID_BYTES\u003e userid{};\n\n\t/* GIVEN that HKDF-SHA256 will fail. */\n\tmock_ctrl_fpsensor_crypto.output_type \u003d\n\t\tMOCK_CTRL_FPSENSOR_CRYPTO_HKDF_SHA256_TYPE_FAIL;\n\n\t/* THEN the derivation will fail with EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN. */\n\tTEST_EQ(derive_encryption_key(unused_key, unused_salt, userid,\n\t\t\t\t      default_fake_tpm_seed),\n\t\tEC_ERROR_UNKNOWN, \"%d\");\n\n\t/* GIVEN that HKDF-SHA256 will succeed after resetting the mock. */\n\tmock_ctrl_fpsensor_crypto \u003d MOCK_CTRL_DEFAULT_FPSENSOR_CRYPTO;\n\n\t/* THEN the derivation will succeed. */\n\tTEST_EQ(derive_encryption_key(unused_key, unused_salt, userid,\n\t\t\t\t      default_fake_tpm_seed),\n\t\tEC_SUCCESS, \"%d\");\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\nAnd register `RUN_TEST(test_derive_encryption_key_failure_hkdf_fail);` in `run_test()`.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/5c6f0d61-fa83-4b3e-acae-7ed55e49cc1e)",
